40 min
MODULE 1.2
Your global-ready profile: CV, LinkedIn, and proof
The international CV
•Two pages maximum. Reverse chronological. PDF, 
named Firstname-Lastname-CV.pdf.
•No photo, date of birth, marital status, state of origin, 
or religion — UK and US employers treat these as red 
flags, not context.
•Every bullet = action + scope + result with a number. 
'Prepared monthly management accounts for a ₦2bn 
loan book; cut reporting time by 30%.'
•NYSC year is real experience: state the PPA, the 
function, and what you delivered.
•Credentials block near the top: qualification, awarding 
body, membership number, year.
LinkedIn that employers read
•Headline = role + credential, not 'Corps member'. 
'KYC/AML Analyst · ACAMS (in progress) · Financial 
crime compliance'.
•About section: 3 short paragraphs — what you do, 
proof, what you want. Written in first person.
•Professional photo: plain background, shoulders up, 
neutral expression, good light.
•Custom URL, location set to Lagos (or your city), 
open-to-work visible to recruiters only.
•Comment substantively on posts in your field twice a 
week — that is how you get found.
Proof that survives verification
•Scan certificates, transcripts, and membership cards 
into one indexed PDF.
•Two referees who can be reached by email and phone 
— tell them first.
•A portfolio of work: a reconciled ledger template, a 
dashboard, a policy summary, a repository. Anonymise 
client data.
•Consistent name and dates across CV, LinkedIn, 
certificates, and passport. One mismatch fails 
verification.
•Professional email: firstname.lastname@ — never a 
nickname or a number string.
Get Global Workforce Ready  ·  NYSC Corps Member Pathway7

30 min
MODULE 1.3
Communicating with global teams: say less, mean more
UK and US workplaces are low-context: the words carry the meaning, hierarchy is soft, and directness is respect. These habits are not wrong in Nigeria — they simply 
do not translate.
Instead ofWrite or sayWhy it matters
"Kindly do the needful.""Could you approve the invoice by Thursday?"Names the action, the owner, and the deadline.
"Good morning sir / ma. I hope this mail finds you well.""Hi Sarah, quick update on the Q3 reconciliation:"First names are standard, even for the CEO. Lead with the point.
"I will revert.""I'll send the figures by 3pm your time."A commitment with a time beats a promise without one.
Silence when stuck"I'm blocked on X. I've tried A and B. Can you point me to C?"Asking early is competence; asking late is a risk to the team.
"It has been done.""Done — file is in the shared folder, link below."Show the evidence. Passive voice hides who did what.
Long formal paragraphs in chatOne line, a bullet list, a clear askSlack and Teams reward brevity and scannability.
