60 min
MODULE 3.5 · LIVE PRACTICAL
One hour on Google Meet: rehearse the real thing
A live session with Deeptalent facilitators — the first time you will be assessed doing the job, not 
describing it. Cameras on, mics ready, screen-share tested.
00–10
Join & tech check
Everyone joins 5 minutes early. Facilitator checks camera, audio, lighting, 
and name format ('Firstname Lastname · KYC'). This is Module 3.3's video 
setup, graded live.
10–25
Live stand-up round
Each learner delivers a 3-line stand-up (Yesterday / Today / Blockers) for a 
given brief, in under 60 seconds, to the room. Peers score point-first, 
number, pace.
25–40
AI task, screen shared
In breakout rooms of three: summarise a 4-page document with an AI tool, 
verify two facts against source, and present the checked result. One person 
shares screen; the others review.
40–52
Mock client interview
Facilitator plays a UK COO. Two volunteers answer two STAR questions each 
while the room observes. Immediate feedback on structure and evidence.
52–60
Ask a placed professional
A Deeptalent professional already working with a UK or US client joins for 
Q&A: first 30 days, time zones, what they would do differently.
GOOGLE MEET LOGISTICS
•Meet link and calendar invite sent 24 hours ahead, stated 
in Lagos time (WAT) and in the facilitator's time zone.
•Laptop, not phone. Wired earphones with mic. Backup 
hotspot tested before joining.
•Camera on for the full hour; blur or plain background; 
display name as instructed.
•Session is recorded for assessment — consent is confirmed 
in the invite.
•Attendance and participation count toward the capstone; a 
missed session is rescheduled once.
•Google Meet is also the tool most UK SME clients use for 
interviews — treat this as your first one.
